<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<div style=""><font face="arial" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">Search NEXUS for <a href="https://nexus.insperity.com/groups/38653/series/3265244-optum-disaster-recovery-resources-bulletins">Optum Disaster Flyer</a> specifically related to incident prompting this template Delete this before sending</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>Dear <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">Client</span>,</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial">In a disaster or emergency, it is important to have a coordinated action plan that is well defined and communicated to all employees. Below are suggestions and resources to help support you in the development of an Emergency and Disaster Preparedness plan for your company. I've also linked the <a href="https://www.insperity.com/magazine/crisis-management-issue-12/">Insperity guide to crisis management</a> as a helpful resource for you.</font></div><div style=""><ol><li><font face="arial">Prepare your teams.</font></li></ol></div><div style=""><ul><li><font face="arial">Develop a Business Emergency Plan</font></li><ul><li><font face="arial">Consider forming a Disaster team responsible for the oversight of plan development, with members tasked with responsibilities prior, during, and post disaster.&nbsp;</font></li></ul></ul></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><span style="white-space:pre">	</span>2. Communicate the Plan.</font></div><div style=""><ul><li><font face="arial">Disseminate information to your employees, steps the company is taking, expectations for work and other plans.&nbsp;</font></li><li><font face="arial">Provide information regarding actions employees can take to prepare themselves and their families prior to, during, and after a disastrous event.</font></li></ul></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><span style="white-space:pre">	</span>3. Restore Business Operations.</font></div><div style=""><ul><li><font face="arial">Assess your employee needs.Respond to employee concerns.</font></li><ul><li><font face="arial">Insperity provides all worksite employees access to Optum, an employee assistance program. Insperity's dedicated phone line at Optum is <b>866-402-0003</b>. We strongly encourage employees to use this free resource to help them with confidential support, counseling, resources and referrals as they work through issues that may arise after a disaster.</font></li></ul></ul></div><div style=""><ul><li><font face="arial">Asses your business needs such as location damage, access to property, etc.&nbsp;</font></li><ul><li><font face="arial">Consider alternate ways of conducting business such as flexible work schedules and telecommuting.</font></li></ul></ul></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>You can also access business and personal preparedness resources through the U.S. Department of Homeland Security's Ready Campaign at <a href="http://www.ready.gov/">Ready.gov.</a></font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>Your Insperity service team is here to help. Please feel welcome to reach out to me with any questions or concerns.&nbsp;</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>We hope you remain safe.</font></div><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>Sincerely,</font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>